# Profile PNG — Instructions

> **Note:** GitHub renders SVG images directly, so all the animated identity SVGs (`profile-avatar.svg`, `ai-identity-core.svg`, `hologram-avatar.svg`, `profile-frame.svg`) work immediately without this file.

A static `profile.png` is provided as a **fallback / social preview** for platforms that do not render SVG (e.g., email signatures, external sites, or as a GitHub social preview image).

## Option A — Generate from the SVG (Recommended)
Open any of the new SVG files in a browser and screenshot the result, or use a converter:

```bash
# ImageMagick example (render frame SVG to PNG)
convert assets/profile-frame.svg -resize 400x400 assets/profile.png
```

## Option B — Use your GitHub avatar directly
GitHub already serves your profile photo at:
```
https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254927016?v=4
```

## Recommended spec
| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Size | 400×400 px (square) |
| Format | PNG (transparent or dark bg) |
| File size | < 1 MB |

## Customization
Download/copy your preferred PNG to `assets/profile.png`. The README can reference it with:
```md
![Profile](assets/profile.png)
